{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791629946,"nonce":"+LIhA8s+kxKx/Q9P/yKtxuzvN9s=","title":"Whether a node is in view, from LayoutContext","message":"The in-view test (inside the root and every clipping ancestor, scrolled and moved by layout animations; hidden or display: none ancestors out) is only reachable through the HashLink entry point, hl_blinc_tree_in_view. A host on LayoutContext, which culls motion that is out of view, needs it too.\n\nMove the body into Tree::in_view, have the HashLink entry point call it, and add LayoutContext::in_view(node).","files":null}]}